<title>USA: CoreComm Q1 shr loss $0.26 vs profit $0.09.</title>
<headline>CoreComm Q1 shr loss $0.26 vs profit $0.09.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>CoreComm Inc</p>
<p>					   Operating results</p>
<p>					  Three Months Ended March 31</p>
<p>							1997	  1996</p>
<p>			   (In thousands, except subscribers, pagers</p>
<p>				    in use, and per share data)</p>
<p> Shr before extraordinary item	  $    .03    $     .09</p>
<p>   Extraordinary item			  (.29)	     --</p>
<p> Net shr (loss)				  (.26)	    .09</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			   (3,426)	  1,289</p>
<p> Revenues					 32,492	 26,796</p>
<p> Operating income			     10,553	  9,264</p>
<p> Weighted average shares		    13,071	 13,932</p>
<p>NOTES: CoreComm said it recorded an extraordinary loss of $4 million ($3.8 million, net of income tax benefit) from the write-off of unamortized deferred financing costs. It said service revs rose to $33.4 million from $28.5 million due to subscriber growth. Subscribers rose to 166,600 from 127,000. Average monthly rev per cellular subscriber decreased to $68 from $78 a year ago. Pagers in use rose to 35,100 from 17,800.</p>
